(7,'Business Analytics Internship','business-analytics-internship','<p>MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation offers a <strong>Business Analytics Internship</strong> designed to equip students and professionals with data-driven decision-making skills. This internship focuses on analyzing business data, identifying trends, generating insights, and supporting strategic business decisions using modern analytical tools and techniques.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>ðŸŽ¯ Internship Objectives</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>To develop analytical and critical thinking skills</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>To understand how data drives business decisions</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>To gain hands-on experience with real-world business datasets</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>To prepare interns for roles in business analytics, data analysis, and consulting</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>ðŸ“š Internship Curriculum</h2>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 1: Introduction to Business Analytics</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Understanding Business Analytics</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Types of Analytics (Descriptive, Diagnostic, Predictive, Prescriptive)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Role of Business Analysts in Organizations</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Data-Driven Decision Making</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 2: Data Fundamentals</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Data Types &amp; Sources</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Data Collection Techniques</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Data Cleaning &amp; Preparation</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Understanding Structured &amp; Unstructured Data</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 3: Tools &amp; Technologies</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>MS Excel for Data Analysis</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Data Visualization Basics</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Introduction to SQL</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Overview of Analytics Tools (Power BI / Tableau &ndash; basics)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 4: Business Data Analysis</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Analyzing Sales, Marketing &amp; Financial Data</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Customer Behavior Analysis</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>KPI &amp; Metrics Analysis</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Trend &amp; Pattern Identification</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 5: Data Visualization &amp; Reporting</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Creating Dashboards &amp; Reports</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Charts, Graphs &amp; Visual Storytelling</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Presenting Insights to Stakeholders</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Business Reporting Best Practices</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 6: Advanced Analytics Concepts</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Basics of Predictive Analytics</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Introduction to Statistical Analysis</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Forecasting &amp; Business Insights</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Risk &amp; Performance Analysis</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 7: Live Business Analytics Project</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Real-World Business Case Study</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Problem Identification &amp; Data Analysis</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Insight Generation &amp; Recommendations</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Final Project Presentation &amp; Evaluation</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>ðŸ› ï¸ What You Will Learn</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>âœ” Business Data Analysis Techniques<br />\r\nâœ” Excel &amp; Data Visualization Skills<br />\r\nâœ” SQL Basics for Analytics<br />\r\nâœ” Dashboard Creation &amp; Reporting<br />\r\nâœ” Business Problem-Solving Skills<br />\r\nâœ” Analytical &amp; Critical Thinking<br />\r\nâœ” Data Interpretation for Decision Making</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>ðŸŽ What You Will Get</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>ðŸ“œ <strong>Internship Completion Certificate</strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>ðŸ† <strong>Project Completion Certificate</strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>ðŸ§  Hands-on Experience with Business Data</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>ðŸ’¼ Career Guidance &amp; Mentorship</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>ðŸ“Š Real Analytics Projects for Portfolio</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>ðŸš€ Improved Career Opportunities in Analytics &amp; Business Domains</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>ðŸ‘©&zwj;ðŸŽ“ Who Can Apply</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Students from Management, Commerce, IT, or Any Stream</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Beginners interested in Business Analytics</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Aspiring Business Analysts &amp; Data Analysts</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Anyone looking to enhance data-driven skills</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>â³ Internship Duration</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Flexible Duration (4 Weeks / 6 Weeks / 8 Weeks)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Mode: Online / Offline (as per availability)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',3,'Months','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1770459479.jpg','Business Analytics Internship 2026 | Excel & Power BI','Business Analytics Internship 2026 with Excel, Power BI and real business case studies.','business analytics internship, power bi internship, excel analytics training',1,'2026-02-07 10:17:59','2026-02-12 06:54:18'),
(8,'Cyber Security ','cyber-security-','<p>The <strong>Cyber Security Internship</strong> is designed for students and freshers who want to build a strong foundation in information security, ethical hacking, and cyber defense. This program focuses on real-world security threats, practical tools, and hands-on learning to prepare interns for careers in cyber security and IT security roles.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h3>Internship Curriculum &amp; What You Will Learn</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Fundamentals of Cyber Security &amp; Information Security</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Networking Basics (TCP/IP, DNS, HTTP/HTTPS)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Linux &amp; Windows Security Fundamentals</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Ethical Hacking Concepts &amp; Methodologies</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Web Application Security &amp; OWASP Top 10</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Vulnerability Assessment &amp; Penetration Testing (VAPT)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Malware, Phishing &amp; Social Engineering Attacks</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Cyber Laws, Digital Forensics &amp; Compliance Basics</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Security Tools (Nmap, Wireshark, Burp Suite, Metasploit &ndash; basics)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Real-world case studies and security breach analysis</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h3>Practical Exposure</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Hands-on labs and simulated cyber attack scenarios</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Live demonstrations of hacking techniques (ethical use only)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Vulnerability scanning and reporting</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Security assessment of websites and systems</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Mini project based on real cyber security problems</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h3>Who Can Apply</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Students pursuing IT, CS, BCA, MCA, or related fields</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Beginners interested in cyber security &amp; ethical hacking</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Anyone passionate about protecting systems and data</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h3>What You Will Get</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Internship Completion Certificate</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Letter of Recommendation (based on performance)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Hands-on practical experience</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Industry-relevant skills &amp; tools knowledge</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Career guidance and cyber security roadmap</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Opportunity to work on real-time projects</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h3>Career Opportunities After Internship</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Cyber Security Analyst</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Ethical Hacker</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>SOC Analyst</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Penetration Tester (Junior Level)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Information Security Executive</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',45,'Days','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771050790.jpg','','','',1,'2026-02-14 06:33:10','2026-02-14 06:33:10'),
(9,'Artifical Intelligence Internship','artifical-intelligence-internship','<p>The <strong>Artificial Intelligence (AI) Internship</strong> at <strong>MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation</strong> is designed to introduce students to the rapidly growing world of AI and intelligent systems. This internship focuses on building a strong foundation in AI concepts with hands-on practical learning, real-world use cases, and industry-oriented projects. It is ideal for students who want to explore how machines learn, think, and make decisions.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h3>Internship Curriculum &amp; What You Will Learn</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Introduction to Artificial Intelligence &amp; Machine Learning</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Python Programming for AI</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Data Handling &amp; Preprocessing</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Supervised &amp; Unsupervised Learning Concepts</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Introduction to Neural Networks &amp; Deep Learning</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Natural Language Processing (NLP) Basics</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Computer Vision Fundamentals</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>AI Algorithms &amp; Model Evaluation</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Working with popular AI libraries (NumPy, Pandas, Scikit-learn &ndash; basics)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Ethical AI, Bias &amp; Responsible AI Practices</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h3>Practical Exposure</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Hands-on coding sessions in Python</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Building simple AI &amp; ML models</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Working with real-world datasets</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Mini projects based on real-life AI applications</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Case studies on AI use in healthcare, finance, education &amp; social development</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h3>Who Can Apply</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Students from BCA, MCA, B.Tech, B.Sc, or related fields</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Beginners interested in Artificial Intelligence &amp; Machine Learning</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Anyone passionate about data-driven decision making and smart technologies</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h3>What You Will Get</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Internship Completion Certificate from <strong>MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation</strong></p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Letter of Recommendation (performance-based)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Practical project experience</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Strong foundation in AI concepts</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Career guidance &amp; future learning roadmap</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Exposure to real-world AI use cases</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h3>Career Opportunities After Internship</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>AI Engineer (Entry Level)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Machine Learning Engineer</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Data Analyst</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>AI Research Assistant</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Python Developer (AI Domain)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',45,'Days','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771050913.webp','','','',1,'2026-02-14 06:35:13','2026-02-14 06:35:13'),
(10,'Advance Excel Internship','advance-excel-internship','<h3><strong>Advanced Excel Internship Program</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation</strong> offers a <strong>structured Advanced Excel Internship</strong> designed to provide practical exposure to <strong>data management, analysis, reporting,</strong> and<strong> automation techniques</strong>. This program focuses on<strong> real-world Excel applications</strong> used in <strong>business environments, helping interns build analytical skills</strong> and <strong>improve decision-making through data</strong>.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>ðŸŽ¯ Internship Objectives</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>To understand advanced Excel tools and functions</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>To develop practical data analysis skills</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>To learn business reporting and dashboard creation</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>To gain hands-on experience with real-world datasets</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>ðŸ“š Internship Curriculum</h2>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 1: Advanced Excel Fundamentals</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Excel Interface &amp; Advanced Features</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Cell Referencing (Absolute, Relative, Mixed)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Data Formatting &amp; Shortcuts</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Working with Large Datasets</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 2: Advanced Formulas &amp; Functions</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Logical Functions (IF, IFS, AND, OR)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Lookup Functions (VLOOKUP, HLOOKUP, XLOOKUP)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>INDEX &amp; MATCH</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>COUNTIF, SUMIF, COUNTIFS, SUMIFS</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Text Functions (LEFT, RIGHT, MID, CONCAT, TRIM)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 3: Data Management &amp; Validation</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Sorting &amp; Advanced Filtering</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Data Validation Techniques</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Removing Duplicates</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Conditional Formatting</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Text to Columns &amp; Flash Fill</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 4: Pivot Tables &amp; Pivot Charts</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Creating Pivot Tables</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Grouping &amp; Summarizing Data</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Using Slicers</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Pivot Charts &amp; Reporting</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 5: Data Analysis Tools</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>What-If Analysis</p>\r\n\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>\r\n		<p>Goal Seek</p>\r\n		</li>\r\n		<li>\r\n		<p>Scenario Manager</p>\r\n		</li>\r\n		<li>\r\n		<p>Data Tables</p>\r\n		</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Basic Statistical Analysis</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Error Handling (IFERROR)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 6: Dashboard Creation</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>KPI Reports</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Dynamic Charts</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Interactive Dashboards</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Report Design &amp; Layout</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 7: Macros &amp; Automation</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Introduction to Macros</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Recording Macros</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Basic VBA Concepts</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Automating Repetitive Tasks</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>ðŸ”¹ Module 8: Live Excel Project</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Business Data Analysis Project</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Report &amp; Dashboard Development</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Data Cleaning &amp; Automation</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Final Project Presentation</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>ðŸ› ï¸ Key Learning Outcomes</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>âœ” Advanced Excel Functions<br />\r\nâœ” Data Cleaning &amp; Management<br />\r\nâœ” Pivot Tables &amp; Reporting<br />\r\nâœ” Dashboard Development<br />\r\nâœ” Automation using Macros<br />\r\nâœ” Business Data Analysis<br />\r\nâœ” Practical Excel Application</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>ðŸŽ What You Will Receive</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>ðŸ“œ Internship Completion Certificate<br />\r\nðŸ† Project Completion Certificate<br />\r\nðŸ“Š Hands-on Excel Experience<br />\r\nðŸ’¼ Career Guidance &amp; Mentorship<br />\r\nðŸ“ Business Report &amp; Dashboard for Portfolio<br />\r\nðŸš€ Enhanced Career Opportunities in Finance, MIS &amp; Data Analysis</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>ðŸ‘©&zwj;ðŸŽ“ Eligibility</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Students from any stream but 12th passed</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Beginners with basic Excel and Mathematical&nbsp;knowledge</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Commerce &amp; Management Students</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Aspiring Data Analysts &amp; MIS Executives</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>â³ Internship Duration</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>4 Weeks / 6 Weeks / 8 Weeks (Flexible)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Mode: Online / Offline (Subject to Availability)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',45,'Days','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771068087.png','','','',1,'2026-02-14 11:21:27','2026-02-14 11:21:27'),
(11,'Social Media for Social Impact Internship Program','social-media-internship','<h2>Program Overview</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>This internship is designed to train students in using social media platforms for awareness campaigns and social causes. Students will learn content creation, campaign planning, and digital engagement while working on real social impact projects.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Internship Curriculum &amp; What You Will Learn</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Introduction to Social Media Strategy</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Content Writing &amp; Canva Designing</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Campaign Planning &amp; Execution</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Hashtag &amp; Audience Research</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Social Media Analytics Basics</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Ethical Digital Communication</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Practical Exposure</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Creating awareness posts</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Designing campaign creatives</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Mini social media projects</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Final campaign submission</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Who Can Apply</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Students from any stream interested in digital marketing and social awareness.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What You Will Get</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Internship Certificate</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Letter of Recommendation (Performance-Based)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Live Project Experience</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',3,'Months','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771580679.png','','','',1,'2026-02-20 09:44:39','2026-02-20 09:44:39'),
(12,'NGO Management & Community Development Internship','ngo-management-community-development-internship','<h2>Internship Title</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Certified NGO Management &amp; Community Development Internship</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Program Overview</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>This internship introduces students to NGO operations, fundraising basics, and community development strategies through practical learning and social research projects.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Curriculum</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>NGO Structure &amp; Operations</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Fundraising Basics</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Community Engagement</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Project Planning</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Awareness Campaign Strategy</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Practical Exposure</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Research on social issues</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Campaign planning</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Community project proposal</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Who Can Apply</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Students interested in social work and public service.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What You Get</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Certificate, LOR, NGO project exposure.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',3,'Months','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771580924.png','','','',1,'2026-02-20 09:48:44','2026-02-20 09:49:29'),
(13,'Rural Education Development Internship','rural-education-development-internship','<h2>Program Overview</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Focused on improving educational awareness in rural areas through digital support, content creation, and career guidance initiatives.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Curriculum</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Rural Education Challenges</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Teaching Assistance Basics</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Study Material Preparation</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Career Awareness Programs</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Government Scheme Awareness</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Practical Exposure</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Creating study resources</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Awareness campaigns</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Educational survey projects</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Who Can Apply</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Students passionate about education &amp; social development.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What You Get</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Certificate, LOR, Social Impact Experience.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',3,'Months','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771581105.png','','','',1,'2026-02-20 09:51:45','2026-02-20 09:51:45'),
(14,'Environmental Sustainability Internship','environmental-sustainability-internship','<h2>Program Overview</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>This internship focuses on climate awareness, sustainability practices, and environmental campaign development.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Curriculum</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Climate Change Basics</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Waste Management Awareness</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Sustainability Campaign Design</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Green Initiatives Planning</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Practical Exposure</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Environmental awareness project</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Research assignments</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Campaign planning</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Who Can Apply</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Students interested in environment &amp; sustainability.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What You Get</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Certificate, LOR, Sustainability project experience.</p>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',3,'Months','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771581203.png','','','',1,'2026-02-20 09:53:23','2026-02-20 09:53:23'),
(15,'Women Empowerment Internship','women-empowerment-internship','<h2>Program Overview</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Promotes awareness on women safety, equality, and leadership through digital campaigns and research-based projects.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Curriculum</h2>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Gender Equality Concepts</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Awareness Campaign Planning</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Community Outreach Strategy</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Policy Awareness</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Practical Exposure</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Campaign creation &amp; awareness content.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Who Can Apply</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Students interested in social change.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What You Get</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Certificate &amp; LOR.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',3,'Months','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771581277.png','','','',1,'2026-02-20 09:54:37','2026-02-20 09:54:37'),
(16,'Youth Leadership & Social Entrepreneurship Internship','youth-leadership-social-entrepreneurship-internship','<h2>Program Overview</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The Youth Leadership &amp; Social Entrepreneurship Internship at MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation is designed to develop leadership qualities and entrepreneurial thinking among students. This internship focuses on building confidence, communication skills, problem-solving ability, and the mindset required to create social impact initiatives.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Students will learn how to lead teams, plan community projects, and design innovative solutions for social challenges through practical assignments and real-world case studies.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Internship Curriculum &amp; What You Will Learn</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Introduction to Leadership &amp; Personality Development</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Communication &amp; Public Speaking Skills</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Team Management &amp; Collaboration</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Basics of Social Entrepreneurship</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Identifying Social Problems &amp; Designing Solutions</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Project Planning &amp; Execution Strategy</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Fundraising &amp; Resource Management Basics</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Ethical Leadership &amp; Responsible Decision Making</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Practical Exposure</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Leadership skill-building activities</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Group project planning exercises</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Case studies on successful social entrepreneurs</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Designing a social initiative proposal</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Final project submission based on a real social issue</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Who Can Apply</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Students from any stream (BBA, BCA, BA, B.Com, B.Tech, etc.)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Beginners interested in leadership &amp; entrepreneurship</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Students preparing for management or government careers</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anyone passionate about creating positive social change</p>\r\n\r\n<p>No prior experience required</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>What You Will Get</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Internship Completion Certificate from MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Letter of Recommendation (Performance-Based)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Practical Leadership &amp; Project Experience</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Entrepreneurial Mindset Development</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Career Guidance &amp; Resume Enhancement Support</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Career Opportunities After Internship</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Team Leader / Project Coordinator</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Social Entrepreneur</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Community Program Manager</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Business Development Executive</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Startup Founder (Social Impact Domain)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>NGO Project Assistant</p>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',3,'Months','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771581483.png','','','',1,'2026-02-20 09:58:03','2026-02-20 09:58:03'),
(17,'Mental Health Awareness & Advocacy Internship','mental-health-awareness-advocacy-internship','<h2>Program Overview</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The Mental Health Awareness &amp; Advocacy Internship at MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation is designed to educate students about mental health issues and promote awareness through responsible digital campaigns and community initiatives. This internship focuses on understanding mental well-being, reducing stigma, and creating impactful awareness strategies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Students will gain practical knowledge about mental health concepts and learn how to design advocacy campaigns that encourage positive conversations and support systems.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Internship Curriculum &amp; What You Will Learn</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Introduction to Mental Health &amp; Emotional Well-being</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Understanding Stress, Anxiety &amp; Depression (Basic Concepts)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Mental Health Awareness Campaign Planning</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Digital Advocacy &amp; Responsible Communication</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Community Engagement Strategies</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Survey Creation &amp; Data Collection Basics</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Ethical Guidelines in Mental Health Communication</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Promoting Positive Mindset &amp; Support Systems</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Practical Exposure</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Creating awareness posters &amp; social media content</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Designing mental health campaigns</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Conducting basic surveys on student well-being</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Case studies on real-life advocacy initiatives</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Final awareness project submission</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Who Can Apply</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Students from any stream (BBA, BCA, BA, B.Com, B.Tech, etc.)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Students interested in psychology &amp; social work</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anyone passionate about promoting mental well-being</p>\r\n\r\n<p>No prior experience required</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>What You Will Get</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Internship Completion Certificate from MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Letter of Recommendation (Performance-Based)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Practical Campaign Experience</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Knowledge of Mental Health Awareness Strategies</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Career Guidance &amp; Resume Enhancement Support</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Career Opportunities After Internship</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Mental Health Awareness Volunteer</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Community Outreach Coordinator</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Social Campaign Executive</p>\r\n\r\n<p>NGO Project Assistant</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Student Wellness Coordinator</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Public Awareness Advocate</p>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',3,'Months','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771581664.png','','','',1,'2026-02-20 10:01:04','2026-02-20 10:01:04'),
(18,'Digital Literacy & Cyber Awareness Internship','digital-literacy-cyber-awareness-internship','<h2>Program Overview</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The Digital Literacy &amp; Cyber Awareness Internship at MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation is designed to educate students about safe and responsible use of digital technologies. This internship focuses on building awareness about cyber security, online privacy, and digital safety while promoting digital literacy in communities.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Students will learn how to create awareness campaigns on cyber safety, identify common online threats, and promote responsible digital behavior through practical projects and real-world case studies.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Internship Curriculum &amp; What You Will Learn</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Introduction to Digital Literacy &amp; Online Safety</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Understanding Cyber Threats (Phishing, Hacking, Scams &ndash; Basics)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Cyber Security Awareness &amp; Data Protection</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Safe Social Media Practices</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Digital Footprint &amp; Online Reputation Management</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Cyber Law &amp; Ethical Digital Usage (Basic Concepts)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Planning &amp; Executing Cyber Awareness Campaigns</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Community Education &amp; Digital Responsibility</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Practical Exposure</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Designing cyber awareness posters &amp; content</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Creating digital safety campaigns</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Case studies on real cyber incidents</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Preparing a digital literacy awareness project</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Final campaign-based project submission</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Who Can Apply</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Students from any stream (BBA, BCA, BA, B.Com, B.Tech, etc.)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Beginners interested in cyber security &amp; digital education</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Students preparing for IT or government careers</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anyone interested in promoting safe digital practices</p>\r\n\r\n<p>No prior experience required</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>What You Will Get</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Internship Completion Certificate from MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Letter of Recommendation (Performance-Based)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Practical Experience in Cyber Awareness Campaigns</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Knowledge of Online Safety &amp; Digital Responsibility</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Career Guidance &amp; Resume Enhancement Support</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Career Opportunities After Internship</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Cyber Awareness Volunteer</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Digital Safety Trainer</p>\r\n\r\n<p>IT Support Assistant (Entry Level)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Cyber Security Executive (Beginner Level)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Community Digital Educator</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Online Safety Campaign Coordinator</p>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',3,'Months','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771581786.png','','','',1,'2026-02-20 10:03:06','2026-02-20 10:03:06'),
(19,'Public Policy & Government Scheme Awareness Internship','public-policy-government-scheme-awareness-internship','<h2>Program Overview</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The Public Policy &amp; Government Scheme Awareness Internship at MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation is designed to help students understand how public policies are formed and how government schemes impact society. This internship focuses on researching government initiatives, simplifying policy information, and creating awareness campaigns to educate communities.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Students will gain practical knowledge of policy analysis and learn how to communicate complex government schemes in a simple and impactful manner.</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Internship Curriculum &amp; What You Will Learn</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Introduction to Public Policy &amp; Governance</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Understanding Central &amp; State Government Schemes</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Policy Research &amp; Data Collection Basics</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Simplifying Policy Information for Public Awareness</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Awareness Campaign Planning &amp; Execution</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Community Outreach &amp; Digital Advocacy</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Basic Report Writing &amp; Documentation</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Ethical Communication &amp; Responsible Information Sharing</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Practical Exposure</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Research on selected government schemes</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Creating simplified awareness content</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Designing public information campaigns</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Case studies on policy implementation</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Final project submission based on a selected scheme</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Who Can Apply</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Students from any stream (BBA, BA, B.Com, BCA, B.Tech, etc.)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Students preparing for government exams</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Anyone interested in public administration &amp; social development</p>\r\n\r\n<p>No prior experience required</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>What You Will Get</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Internship Completion Certificate from MG Education &amp; Social Development Organisation</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Letter of Recommendation (Performance-Based)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Practical Experience in Policy Research &amp; Awareness</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Skill Development in Public Communication</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Career Guidance &amp; Resume Enhancement Support</p>\r\n\r\n<hr />\r\n<h2>Career Opportunities After Internship</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Public Policy Assistant</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Government Scheme Coordinator</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Research Intern</p>\r\n\r\n<p>NGO Policy Support Executive</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Community Outreach Officer</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Social Development Project Assistant</p>\r\n','{\"amount\":\"1500\",\"description\":\"\"}',3,'Months','assets/uploads/internships/internship_1771581840.png','','','',1,'2026-02-20 10:04:00','2026-02-20 10:04:00');
